            <ArticleTitle>Acne fulminans with prolonged polyarthralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 19-year-old man with acne fulminans found that his prolonged polyarthralgia was controlled by nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory agents. HLA typing showed the presence of A2, B7, and B8 antigens.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
